<title>NORWAY: Aker Maritime says UK oil project on time.</title>
<headline>Aker Maritime says UK oil project on time.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore company Aker Maritime ASA said on Wednesday a construction job for Texaco Inc's Erskine project in the British sector of the North Sea was approaching completion on target.</p>
<p>Aker's McNulty yard in Newcastle has built the topsides for the unmanned wellhead platform and also a process module for Amoco Corp's nearby Lomond installation.</p>
<p>Both units will be shipped offshore in April, according to the company's Aker Pulse newsletter.</p>
<p>Worth more than 60 million stg, the turnkey contract covered engineering, procurement, construction and installation.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
